Distinguish the following categories:
Canonical story: narrative, dialogue, dreams, letters, decrees, dispatches, chronicles, sermons, treaties, songs, and other in-world text intended to be read as part of the fiction.
River's story prose: passages I wrote as part of the narrative. Preserve these with especially light intervention.
Canonical directives: my out-of-character choices and corrections that establish what happened, even when their words are not themselves story prose. Record these in the canon ledger, not the body of the book.
Editorial or conversational material: planning, assistant preambles, follow-up offers, options, model commentary, metanarrative summaries, and other material not intended for the novel.
Superseded or alternate text: passages explicitly replaced, rejected, or belonging to an unchosen branch. Retain them in the preservation archive, but do not automatically put them in the reading edition.
Uncertain material: passages whose status, order, or wording cannot be established confidently. Preserve them and record the issue.
An earlier passage is superseded only when there is good evidence that River replaced or rejected it, or the accepted continuation clearly adopts a conflicting rewrite. A request for a rewrite may apply to one paragraph rather than the whole scene. Preserve unaffected material. Do not discard an earlier scene simply because a later scene resembles it. If the later version is clearly adopted, use it and preserve the earlier version in the archive. If evidence is equivocal, avoid an irreversible choice, identify the conflicting passages, and continue with unaffected work. Do not use majority frequency as the sole test of canon. River's explicit decisions take precedence over repetition, and later specific corrections generally take precedence over earlier generic statements.
If an important event exists only in a directive or recap, do not silently turn it into newly written narrative and label it recovered prose. Establish whether it is canon and record that a narrative treatment is absent. Ask for the missing passage or separate permission for a new bridge if needed. </source_and_canon_rules>
